# What this repository does and does not carry.
#
# The rule: **track the small, immutable inputs; ignore the large, regenerable
# outputs.** Every ignored path below can be rebuilt by a script in `scripts/`,
# and every tracked path either cannot be, or is small enough that carrying it
# is cheaper than the instructions to recreate it.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The database
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Untracked as of 2026-09-04. It was tracked once, at the initial commit, and
# never updated: the committed copy had four tables while the working copy had
# eight, so a fresh clone got a database the home page could not open. That is
# the worst of both worlds - repository weight *and* a misleading artifact.
#
# It is fully rebuildable: `scripts/build_database.py` takes about two minutes
# from the season CSVs kept below, and build_xg / build_fixtures / build_rosters
# / build_injuries add the rest. `scripts/make_sample_data.py` gets the app
# running with no network at all.
#
# DuckDB files are binary and do not delta-compress, so each commit would store
# a whole fresh copy - roughly 22MB a time, and it changes most sessions.
data/football.duckdb
data/*.duckdb
# The write-ahead log. Present only while a connection is open, never wanted.
data/*.wal

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded caches
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 161MB of Understat JSON and 17MB of injury payloads. Both are third-party API
# responses: reproducible, large, and rewritten constantly. Re-downloading is
# the slow part of a fresh setup (roughly 45 minutes for rosters), which is the
# real cost of ignoring them - accepted deliberately.
data/raw/understat/
data/raw/injuries/

# football-data.co.uk's upcoming-fixtures feed. A few days wide and rewritten
# daily, unlike the season files below.
data/raw/fixtures.csv

# Club badges. Regenerable by `scripts/build_crests.py`, but the reason they
# are ignored is not size (628KB) - it is that they are third-party club
# crests fetched from a provider's CDN, and a public repository should not
# redistribute them. `crests.monogram` means the app still looks finished
# without them.
data/crests/

# Anything a run happens to write into `data/` that is not named above.
data/sample/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, so the reasoning survives
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/raw/<season>/*.csv - the football-data.co.uk season files, ~8MB in
#   total. Small, effectively immutable once a season ends, and they are what
#   makes `build_database.py` work offline. This is the one input that cannot
#   be regenerated if the source ever disappears.
# data/raw/crest_ids.json - a couple of kilobytes of team ids that otherwise
#   cost API-Football requests from a 100-a-day allowance.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and logs
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No .env exists yet, and this is here so that stays true by accident as well
# as on purpose. `FOOTBALL_API_KEY` is read from the environment for exactly
# this reason - a key committed once is in the history for ever.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
